  "title": "Build: University Library Management",
  "type": "build",
  "difficulty": "Intermediate",
  "category": "Freeform Modeling",
  "scenario": "Design a University Library system with two actors: Student (primary) and Librarian (secondary staff). Students \"Borrow Book\". Borrowing a book unconditionally «includes» \"Check Student Fine Balance\". If the student returns a book late during \"Return Book\", they are optionally triggered to \"Pay Overdue Fine\" via «extend».",
  "goal": "Build the entire relationship structure using the canvas tools: connect Student, Librarian, Borrow Book, Return Book, Check Fine Balance, and Pay Overdue Fine.",
  "learningObjective": "Synthesize multiple interconnected use cases with dual actors and distinct include/extend pathways.",
  "hints": [
    "Student associates with \"Borrow Book\" and \"Return Book\".",
    "Librarian is a secondary actor assisting with \"Return Book\" and \"Pay Overdue Fine\".",
    "\"Borrow Book\" includes \"Check Fine Balance\" (arrow points -> Check Fine Balance).",
    "\"Pay Overdue Fine\" extends \"Return Book\" (arrow points from Pay Overdue Fine -> Return Book)."
  ],
  "solutionExplanation": "Real world business workflows often trigger extensions upon exceptional circumstances (like an overdue return requiring a fine payment).",
